/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Varnam is traditionally the central and most elaborate item of a Bharatanatyam recital. It combines Nritta \(pure dance\) and Abhinaya \(expressive storytelling\). It requires considerable stamina, technical skill, and emotional expression. Through intricate rhythmic sequences and expressive passages, dancers communicate complex stories and emotions. Varnams often explore themes of devotion, longing and love, sometimes portraying a devotee's relationship with a deity.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
