/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 85 0 R
/E (Padam is an expressive dance item that focuses primarily on emotions, facial expressions, and storytelling rather than complicated rhythmic movements. The dancer interprets poetic lyrics, often exploring themes such as devotion, love, separation, longing, jealousy, and relationships. Padams allow the dancer to demonstrate their understanding of Abhinaya by portraying different characters, emotions, and situations. They are often performed at a slower pace, giving the audience time to understand the story and its emotional depth.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [7]
>>
