/P 86 0 R
/E (Javali is a lighter form of expressive dance that often explores romantic themes and human relationships. Unlike devotional Padams, Javalis frequently portray everyday romantic situations, such as attraction, affection, playful teasing, and misunderstandings. They are generally performed at a livelier pace and allow the dancer to demonstrate subtle expressions, characterisation and storytelling. Javalis are not compulsory in every Arangetram and may be included depending on the dancer's repertoire and the guru's choice.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
