/E (Tillana is a lively, energetic dance item traditionally performed toward the end of a Bharatanatyam recital. It focuses on intricate rhythmic patterns, fast footwork, coordinated movements, and graceful poses. Its music features rhythmic syllables called Jatis and melodic passages. Although Tillana primarily showcases pure dance, it may also contain a short devotional section towards the end. It allows the dancer to demonstrate their technical precision, stamina, and stage presence.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
